                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Shadows of the Vatican – Act I: Greed is a pretty enjoyable point-and-click adventure with an interesting story and atmosphere. The character animations look poor, even for the game’s age, but the Vatican setting still gives it a unique feel. The puzzles were generally okay and not too difficult. Only a few required a bit of extra thought, but nothing particularly special. They were still enjoyable to solve.\r\n\r\nI also found the achievement farming easy, which is a nice bonus for completionists. Not a perfect game, but definitely worth playing if you enjoy classic adventure games and mystery stories.",
